BESMART Quality Review Tool (QRT), Section III: Appointment Frequency. Changes are effective July 1, 2026. Induction and Stabilization standards have been separated; the stabilization phase standard now reflects the requirement for psychotherapy; phase of treatment must be clearly documented.
Induction Phase (Skip Standards 21-23 ONLY IF documentation of the induction phase is not available):
- Standard 21: A patient in the induction phase of treatment has had: 1. One (1) to three (3) provider appointments scheduled weekly;
- Standard 22: 2. Received counseling at each induction visit. Received other supportive services (as appropriate) at each induction visit, such as; peer support, illness management and recovery, or other health and behavioral management activities;
- Standard 23: 3. Had one (1) observed random drug screen at least weekly.
Stabilization Phase (Skip Standards 24-26 if patient is NOT in the stabilization phase):
- Standard 24: A patient in the stabilization phase of treatment has had: 1. Had a scheduled provider appointment at least every one (1) to three (3) weeks;
- Standard 25: 2. Received psychotherapy at least monthly;
- Standard 26: 3. Had one (1) observed random drug screen at least monthly.

BESMART Quality Review Tool (QRT), Section IV: Service Delivery. Changes are effective July 1, 2026. Training and education is now required to be completed annually; a psychosocial assessment is required within 30 days of treatment initiation.
- Standard 33: There is evidence in the clinical record of patient receiving training and education on the following topics (Note: These must be documented once with initial establishment of care, and annually): (a) Treatment options, including detoxification, benefits/risks associated with each option;
- Standard 34: (b) Risk of neonatal abstinence syndrome for all female patients of childbearing age (ages 15-44);
- Standard 35: (c) Prevention and treatment of chronic viral illnesses, such as HIV and hepatitis C;
- Standard 36: (d) Therapeutic benefits and adverse effects of treatment medication;
- Standard 37: (e) Risks for overdose, and
- Standard 38: (f) Overdose prevention and reversal agents.
- Standard 39: There is evidence that the Controlled Substance Monitoring Database (CSMD) was queried each time and prior to a prescription being ordered (e.g. e-scribed/called in/written).
- Standard 40: A psychosocial assessment was completed within 30-days of treatment initiation, by a qualified professional within the patient's treatment team.
